# File: tests/features/routed-sessions.feature
# Generated from: specs/26-bound-the-routed-in-place-summary-and-clear-the-routed-status-line-on-claude-steps/requirements.md
Feature: Bounded in-place summary and a status line that follows the model

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: A stalled in-place summary times out
    Given "opencode-go/kimi-k3.1-pro" is over the auto-compaction threshold and OpenCode Go accepts the summary request and then sends nothing
    When 120 seconds pass after the summary request is sent
    Then the request is aborted, the routed view is unchanged, the transcript shows "OpenCode Go could not summarize this conversation (timed_out); it will be retried at the next turn end.", and the next routed main-loop step runs

  @SCN006 @regression
  Scenario: A routed step does not wait for a running summary
    Given an in-place summary for "opencode-go/kimi-k3.1-pro" is still running
    When a routed main-loop step starts
    Then the step answers at once with the routed view as it is, and the summary, once it finishes, is sent from the next routed main-loop step

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: A timed-out summary is retried at the next turn end
    Given an in-place summary that timed out
    When the next main-loop turn ends with the context still over the threshold
    Then the in-place summary is sent again

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: A summary within the deadline is kept as before
    Given OpenCode Go returns the summary before 120 seconds pass
    When the in-place summary runs
    Then the summary is kept in the routed view and no timeout line is logged

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: A Claude main-loop step clears the routed status line
    Given a routed main-loop step on "opencode-go/kimi-k3.1-pro" set the status line
    When the next main-loop step runs on "claude-haiku-5-5"
    Then nmg-router's status line is cleared

  @SCN005 @regression
  Scenario: Routed and subagent status behavior is preserved
    Given a routed main loop, and a subagent step on a Claude or routed model
    When each step completes or fails
    Then the routed main-loop step sets the model and thinking status or the error status, and the subagent step leaves the status line as it is
